{"created": "2026-10-24T00:35:25.612245+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-24T00:35:26.843720+00:00", "id": 23607297, "conceptrecid": "23607296", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23607297", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23607296", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23607297", "metadata": {"title": "Per-model language z-scores on LTBv1 (Chinese-source subset): replication package", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23607297", "publication_date": "2026-10-24", "description": "Replication package for the manuscript <i>Accumulating Invisibility: How Platformised AI Translation Converts Cultural Discount into a National-Image Externality</i> (submitted to <i>Global Media and China</i>).\n\n<p><b>Contents.</b> (1) <code>ltb_per_model_zscores.csv</code> - per-model within-model language z-scores computed on the Chinese-source items of the Last Translation Benchmark (LTBv1). 32 rows = 31 machine-translation systems (7 China-developed, 24 non-China-developed) plus one human baseline row, which is excluded from the model-level group comparison reported in the manuscript. Columns: <code>model</code>, <code>origin</code>, <code>zho_n</code> (number of Chinese-source cases scored), <code>within_model_z</code> (within-model standardised pass rate). (2) <code>recompute_from_release.py</code> - a self-contained replication script (Python standard library only, no network access). Run as <code>python recompute_from_release.py</code> on the CSV: it regenerates every figure reported in section 4.2 of the manuscript - China-developed n = 7, mean z = +1.3841, median +1.1851, 7/7 positive; non-China-developed n = 24, mean z = +0.0089, median z = -0.1221 (exact value -0.12215), 9/24 positive; Mann-Whitney U = 156; two-sided exact p = 1.8710e-04 (exact enumeration of all C(31,7) = 2,629,575 splits; no ties). (3) <code>README.md</code> and <code>ATTRIBUTION.md</code> - contents, provenance and licensing.</p>\n\n<p><b>Scope and interpretation.</b> The z-score standardises each model's pass rate on Chinese-source items against that same model's own cross-language pass-rate distribution. It is a capability-consistency diagnostic, not a measure of ideological stance, and it is a model-level statistic rather than a catalogue-level one.</p>\n\n<p><b>Upstream data.</b> This package does not redistribute LTBv1. The underlying benchmark is reported by Zouhar, V. et al. (2026), <i>The Last Translation Benchmark</i>, arXiv:2609.04173; dataset CC BY 4.0 (Hugging Face: zouhar/last-translation-benchmark), code MIT (GitHub: zouharvi/last-translation-benchmark). Only derived measurements are deposited here, under CC BY 4.0.</p>\n\n<p><b>Anonymity.</b> The deposit is made under an anonymous creator name to preserve the journal's double-anonymised review process.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Anonymous", "affiliation": null}], "keywords": ["machine translation", "translation evaluation", "cultural discount", "within-model language z-score", "LTBv1", "Chinese-source translation", "replication package"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.48550/arXiv.2609.04173", "relation": "isDerivedFrom", "scheme": "doi"}], "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23607296"}}]}}, "title": "Per-model language z-scores on LTBv1 (Chinese-source subset): replication package", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23607297", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23607297", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23607297?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23607297", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23607297", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23607297", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23607297/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23607296", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23607296", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10